      "figure": "Figure 4",
      "caption": "Figure 4 : Illustration of our framework for computing visual token information .\nAt the i i -th layer of VLLM’s language decoder, we firstly remove all other visual tokens except the target one and run one forward pass. Next we additionally run another forward pass by further removing the only one visual token. The difference between these two output probabilities on the ground-truth label defines the information score I i ​ ( 𝐕 k ) \\text{I}_{i}(\\mathbf{V}_{k}) .",
