      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1 : Overview of LAOF framework: Consecutive observations ( o t , o t + 1 ) (o_{t},o_{t+1}) and their corresponding RGB-formatted optical flow f rgb , t f_{\\text{rgb},t} are encoded into feature space ( s t , s t + 1 , f t ) (s_{t},s_{t+1},f_{t}) . The inverse and forward dynamics models, along with the flow decoder, are then jointly optimized under the combined supervision of next-state reconstruction and optical flow constraints.",
