  {
    "id": "cvpr26-4ff37da86a0d",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 1",
      "caption": "Figure 1 : Overview of Hybrid Masking Adaptation of LLaDA-V for GUI Grounding. (a) The adapted framework takes a natural-language instruction and a GUI screenshot (either from web, desktop, or mobile interfaces) as input. LLaDA-V trained with the linear masking predicts the action type, optional type_in text, and anchor coordinates ( x 1 , y 1 ) (x_{1},y_{1}) . LLaDA-V model trained with the full deterministic masking predicts the remaining bounding-box coordinates ( x 2 , y 2 ) (x_{2},y_{2}) conditioned on the image, instruction, and anchor.\n(b) Linear Masking Phase: action and anchor tokens in the response are randomly masked according to the linear masking during the forward corruption process during training for coarse grounding during training.\n(c) Deterministic Masking Phase: all response tokens are fully masked in the forward corruption process during training, and LLaDA-V predicts the bounding-box extent during denoising.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2603.26211v1/main_diag.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S0.F1",
