    "id": "cvpr26-13c7412914db",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-13c7412914db",
      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3. Overview of ZOO-Prune. Given visual tokens from the vision encoder, we estimate token sensitivity via zeroth-order gradient approximation at the projection layer by adding Gaussian perturbations (i.e., xi ± huj). The resulting sensitivity scores are integrated with a diversity objective to form a hybrid score, guiding the selection. The selected subset is then passed to the LLM together with the text input, enabling efficient multimodal reasoning with reduced computation.",
      "page": 4,
      "captionRect": [
