    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-232637e80ec7",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of our method. Our GDFA framework op- timizes federated unlearning through geometry-driven directional alignment. Specifically, 1) the global model is migrated to a flat loss region to enhance stability. 2) task vectors generated by rele- vant clients are merged only when their elements share consistent signs, masking conflicting ones. 3) the refined task vector is sub- tracted from the original model via reverse aggregation to erase target knowledge.",
      "page": 4,
      "captionRect": [
