    "id": "cvpr26-997a086be6bd",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-997a086be6bd",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of the proposed pose estimation framework (best viewed in color). (A) General overview. A CNN backbone extracts feature maps F∈RC×H×W . Spatial covariance pooling over the H×W grid gives ˆΣ∈SH×W ++ which is fed to the pose head. (B) Learning the pose. After L geometry-aware layers, the compact SPD matrix ΣL ∈S4 ++ is decoded by a differentiable Cholesky layer into (u, v; t); (u, v) are mapped to SO(3) and the loss is computed on SO(3) × R3. (C) SPD learning layers. Each layer applies a BiMap followed by eigenvalue rectification ReEigε [29] preserving strict positive definiteness.",
      "page": 4,
      "captionRect": [
