    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-cef56aa0e544",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of the CryoKRAQEN architecture. CryoKRAQEN reconstructs heterogeneous 3D structures from noisy cryo-EM images using a quantized triplane-based Fourier codebook. For each particle, a Fourier slice is extracted, compared with image features, and converted into annealed soft assignment weights via an Epanechnikov kernel. These weights combine codebook entries to form the particle’s 3D Fourier volume, which is transformed into a spatial density map. Inference: The learned assignment weights are applied directly to the triplane codebook to generate the corresponding 3D volume and density.",
      "page": 4,
      "captionRect": [
        58.5,
        280.9841003417969,
        553.4990844726562,
        333.86834716796875
