  {
    "id": "cvpr26-5f733d7a874b",
    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Overview of Easy3E.\nThe framework operates in two main stages: Geometry Editing and Texture Refinement.\nStarting from a rendered source view, an edited target image provides the guidance for editing.\nIn the Geometry Editing stage, the Voxel FlowEdit algorithm transforms the source voxel structure under flow-based guidance, followed by SLAT Repainting that refines local latent features to produce the target mesh.\nThe Texture Refinement stage then employs a generation branch and a normal-guided control adapter to synthesize multi-view-consistent textures, which are projected and fused onto the mesh to yield the final high-fidelity 3D asset.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2602.21499v2/pipeline.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S3.F2",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
      "score": 28,
