      "id": "cvpr26-b57d08931c8d",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of our ReasonX framework. (a) We fine-tune an MLLM to judge relative intrinsic properties from RGB images using sampled point pairs. (b) The frozen judge then provides rewards within a GRPO loop to refine an intrinsic decomposition model π: for each RGB image, we generate a group of G = 8 samples, query the judge across point pairs and modalities, and compute group-relative rewards to update π without ground-truth intrinsics.",
