    "id": "cvpr26-c5b987030a57",
    "extraction": {
      "id": "cvpr26-c5b987030a57",
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2. Overview of our TMD method. (a) Decoupled archi- tecture for TMD student, where the main backbone takes the noisy sample xt, timestep t and text conditioning c as inputs and outputs the main feature mt, and with a simple fusion layer, ﬂow head conditions on mt, c and predicts the less noisy target yr from the more noisy ys (s →r). (b) Top: Transition process maps noise to data with a few transition steps. Bottom: In each step, ﬂow head rollout is performed during both distillation and sampling. We omit the timestep inputs s and r to the ﬂow head for simplicity.",
