      "figure": "Figure 3",
      "caption": "Figure 3. Overview of the Batman framework. Malicious knowledge is extracted from the attacker’s local parameters via truncated SVD and the constructed null space, isolating dominant directions responsible for backdoor behavior. Benign knowledge alignment is then projected into the malicious null space to retain attack functionality while improving stealthiness. Details refer to Section 4.",
