    "extraction": {
      "figure": "Figure 2",
      "caption": "Figure 2 : Framework overview. Q, AE and AD represent quantization, arithmetic encoder and decoder, respectively. The input image x t x_{t} is first embedded into patches and then fed into the encoder composed of local and global transformers to produce y t y_{t} . The local transformer handles each window independently with low cost, while the global transformer captures inter-window correlations. Subsequently, an entropy model then performs autoregressive entropy coding on y t y_{t} . The decoder adopts an architecture similar to the encoder to reconstruct the image x ^ t \\hat{x}_{t} . All are guided by a context model combining long-term 1D memory and short-term context buffer to provide comprehensive temporal context.",
      "image_url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2603.15302v1/pipeline.png",
      "figureAnchor": "S2.F2",
      "panelIndex": 0,
      "panelCount": 1,
